From 3e0c1ae2d0d32e6376abebca0f3cc1a032589dd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Genesis builder <builder@genesis.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:18:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] B20_R2 CRPD-1: one soundness-mode record for
 abstractions, transports and bounds

Adopted subset of the CRPD v3 proposal (s3.1), mapped onto the handoff's representation and
world rules (s15.3, s16.2). No new top-level package.

- invention/soundness.py: modes EQ / SUFF / NEC / BOUND / HEURISTIC / REJECTED are derived
  from checked obligations (forward = sufficiency, backward = necessity), never taken from
  the proposer; requested and established modes are kept apart (meet, never upgraded);
  licences per use (order, lift_positive, lift_negative, prune, bound_lower/upper);
  HEURISTIC and REJECTED never admit a proof; an optimum needs matching checked bounds on
  one task and objective; aliasing_refutation turns a checked aliasing pair into a
  disproved direction (the CRPD-4 trigger); VACUOUS for inconsistent worlds.
- Wired in: worlds.judge decisions carry their mode (B18 verdicts unchanged);
  obstruction.record_evidence derives BOUND records from a checker-only replay;
  research.run marks its policy guidance HEURISTIC.
- scripts/b20r_soundness_audit.py -> evidence/soundness_b20r/modes.json: modes of every
  existing artifact from recorded evidence: 5 SUFF, 13 REJECTED, 6 HEURISTIC, 12 BOUND
  (12 optima licensed). No EQ abstraction exists yet.
- tests_formal/test_soundness_modes.py (13 tests): truth table, licensing, tampering,
  bounds/optimum, a degree-sequence aliasing pair for C4, exhaustive codegree check on
  5 vertices (finite evidence, not proof), B18/B20_R1 artifacts, wiring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ee919ZRwjeJ7vDUowbM8dB
